(2118801, 286218, 43753, '<td valign="top">Very powerful statement. I love the contast between the beautiful green countryside with blue sk iverhead and the dingy industrial look of the gat. Nice capture. Excellent title.</td>', 'Very powerful statement. I love the contast between the beautiful green countryside with blue sk iverhead and the dingy industrial look of the gat. Nice capture. Excellent title.', '2006-02-03 15:06:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2118802, 289221, 772, '<td valign="top">This is one of the best photos I have seen in quite a while... excellent work :) 10 +fav</td>', 'This is one of the best photos I have seen in quite a while... excellent work :) 10 +fav', '2006-02-03 15:06:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(2118804, 285922, 43031, '<td valign="top">Street art/photography is not dead or fading. Take a look at pawdrix''s portfolio, or www.chromasia.com (click back through the entire last year, it''s worth it), Or Librodo''s portfolio. <br/> <br/>The problem with this photo is that you abandoned all thought of composition. I have no idea if you had problems with the man and getting his photo. But if he could have been (or was) a willing subject, I think you could have done much more with this. Maybe give him some money to pose or something. <br/> <br/>Anyways, use thirds, symmetry,negative space, or whatever, but this haphazard arrangement takes away from the focal point (the man IMO). I can see many possibilities, but the most obvious to me is stand directly in front of him, him to the left side of the frame, and his table beside him.</td>', 'Street art/photography is not dead or fading. Take a look at pawdrix''s portfolio, or www.chromasia.com (click back through the entire last year, it''s worth it), Or Librodo''s portfolio.  The problem with this photo is that you abandoned all thought of composition. I have no idea if you had problems with the man and getting his photo. But if he could have been (or was) a willing subject, I think you could have done much more with this. Maybe give him some money to pose or something.  Anyways, use thirds, symmetry,negative space, or whatever, but this haphazard arrangement takes away from the focal point (the man IMO). I can see many possibilities, but the most obvious to me is stand directly in front of him, him to the left side of the frame, and his table beside him.', '2006-02-03 15:06:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(2118806, 288307, 43753, '<td valign="top">I like the layers here. There is something interesting to look at all the way through the image, from the water to the mountains. Beautiful.</td>', 'I like the layers here. There is something interesting to look at all the way through the image, from the water to the mountains. Beautiful.', '2006-02-03 15:08:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(2118809, 288936, 43753, '<td valign="top">Nice contrast here. I like the pairing. Great colors and tecture, nice frame.</td>', 'Nice contrast here. I like the pairing. Great colors and tecture, nice frame.', '2006-02-03 15:08:43.000000', NULL, 1),
