(2132107, 287540, 37430, '<td valign="top"><i>Greetings from the Critique Club!</i> <br/> <br/><b>Aesthetic:</b>Though the subject is cute and lovable, the image still lacks a bit on composition. Similar color background, in same tones, is not letting the subject stand out.<br/> <br/><b>Technical:</b>The focus looks a little soft. I guess its more due to tighter crop ...is it? Otherwise it is well exposed picture.<br/> <br/><b>Challenge:</b>Offcourse, Anything would fit in for this challenge theme ...so no comments :)<br/> <br/><b>Conclusion:</b>Oveall an average composition. I feel the background and "similar" tones in whole photo make it difficult for the subject to stand out. I feel if the background was burnt and subject was selectively sharpened in photoshop, it might have added some depth to photo. But for sure- you have eye for "interesting" (in this case, cute) subjects :). You really have some great pictures in your profile and I don''t feel this one really fits into them. Hope this is just an exception :)<br/> <br/>I''m by no means expert in area of photography. My comments are purely based on my limited understanding of technology and art behind digital photography. Apart from doing detailed evaluation of your submission, my intent is to learn different styles  of photography by critically evaluating selective submissions. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via email or PM.<br/> <br/>Wish you a great day!<br/><b><i>-Tej</i></b></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  Aesthetic:Though the subject is cute and lovable, the image still lacks a bit on composition. Similar color background, in same tones, is not letting the subject stand out. Technical:The focus looks a little soft. I guess its more due to tighter crop ...is it? Otherwise it is well exposed picture. Challenge:Offcourse, Anything would fit in for this challenge theme ...so no comments :) Conclusion:Oveall an average composition. I feel the background and "similar" tones in whole photo make it difficult for the subject to stand out. I feel if the background was burnt and subject was selectively sharpened in photoshop, it might have added some depth to photo. But for sure- you have eye for "interesting" (in this case, cute) subjects :). You really have some great pictures in your profile and I don''t feel this one really fits into them. Hope this is just an exception :) I''m by no means expert in area of photography. My comments are purely based on my limited understanding of technology and art behind digital photography. Apart from doing detailed evaluation of your submission, my intent is to learn different styles  of photography by critically evaluating selective submissions. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via email or PM. Wish you a great day!-Tej', '2006-02-08 01:16:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132108, 289002, 39433, '<td valign="top">congrads on the blue, my favorite. This shot is simply great</td>', 'congrads on the blue, my favorite. This shot is simply great', '2006-02-08 01:16:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132133, 287509, 15711, '<td valign="top">Top 50 out of 619.  Not too shabby!!!!!</td>', 'Top 50 out of 619.  Not too shabby!!!!!', '2006-02-08 01:20:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132166, 279484, 33868, '<td valign="top">Not quite sharp enough and generally lacks interest for me anyway.</td>', 'Not quite sharp enough and generally lacks interest for me anyway.', '2006-02-08 01:32:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132171, 287519, 11960, '<td valign="top">I rated this one low for 2 reasons. The first being the lack of sharp focus; the focus is soft, at best. Secondly, was the lack of tonal range. I realize this is a brown, bleak subject anyway, but there just isn''t any *wow* factor to it... Hope this helps!</td>', 'I rated this one low for 2 reasons. The first being the lack of sharp focus; the focus is soft, at best. Secondly, was the lack of tonal range. I realize this is a brown, bleak subject anyway, but there just isn''t any *wow* factor to it... Hope this helps!', '2006-02-08 01:34:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132179, 276358, 37430, '<td valign="top"><i>Greetings from the Critique Club!</i> <br/> <br/>..and this is the first time I got to critique two photos from the same member. Guess what would be the odds of picking two consecutive pictures from 750 in queue and both from the same person!:)<br/> <br/><b>Aesthetic:</b> I love flower shots and I have one for the same challenge myself. This one looks cool. Just white on black with hint of yellow looks cool.<br/> <br/><b>Technical:</b> Some of the detils got missed out for while on white (petals on inside of flower) but overall its well exposed.<br/> <br/><b>Challenge:</b> For sure- it fits the challenge.<br/> <br/><b>Conclusion:</b> This is certainly a lovely picture. There could be few things done to make it even better. One - too bad that the flower on right is cut. Two - follow the rule-of-thirds. Voters love it. Three - I''m not too sure of this one but glow filter might add some punch. I used it on my submission for the same challenge, which was also flowers, and it was positively received by voters. Anyway, some people are of the opinion that filters should be avoided...so dont take my word on this one :)<br/> <br/>..and yes- the bike is still cool (for this critique also as nothing much have happended in ast 10 mins to change my mind for it) :)<br/> <br/>Wish you a great day!<br/><b><i>-Tej</i></b></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  ..and this is the first time I got to critique two photos from the same member. Guess what would be the odds of picking two consecutive pictures from 750 in queue and both from the same person!:) Aesthetic: I love flower shots and I have one for the same challenge myself. This one looks cool. Just white on black with hint of yellow looks cool. Technical: Some of the detils got missed out for while on white (petals on inside of flower) but overall its well exposed. Challenge: For sure- it fits the challenge. Conclusion: This is certainly a lovely picture. There could be few things done to make it even better. One - too bad that the flower on right is cut. Two - follow the rule-of-thirds. Voters love it. Three - I''m not too sure of this one but glow filter might add some punch. I used it on my submission for the same challenge, which was also flowers, and it was positively received by voters. Anyway, some people are of the opinion that filters should be avoided...so dont take my word on this one :) ..and yes- the bike is still cool (for this critique also as nothing much have happended in ast 10 mins to change my mind for it) :) Wish you a great day!-Tej', '2006-02-08 01:36:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132187, 287519, 21816, '<td valign="top">I have to agree with tryal15 here I''m afraid. The lack of sharpness in the photo is what grabs me first here. Maybe you could of used some slight dodging effects just to enhance the tonal range a little throughout the picture?</td>', 'I have to agree with tryal15 here I''m afraid. The lack of sharpness in the photo is what grabs me first here. Maybe you could of used some slight dodging effects just to enhance the tonal range a little throughout the picture?', '2006-02-08 01:38:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132190, 285757, 27133, '<td valign="top">A huge congrats Elsapo......very creative and brilliant colours.  You got one of my 10 votes for this one.</td>', 'A huge congrats Elsapo......very creative and brilliant colours.  You got one of my 10 votes for this one.', '2006-02-08 01:38:44.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(2132219, 289002, 41746, '<td valign="top">Outstanding shot, Gísli. Innilega til hamingju  með þann bláa!</td>', 'Outstanding shot, Gísli. Innilega til hamingju  með þann bláa!', '2006-02-08 01:46:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132222, 286106, 30861, '<td valign="top">A beautiful piece of work, ZZ. Sadly underrated by the voters.</td>', 'A beautiful piece of work, ZZ. Sadly underrated by the voters.', '2006-02-08 01:46:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132224, 289221, 30214, '<td valign="top">fantastic shot, skip! congrats!</td>', 'fantastic shot, skip! congrats!', '2006-02-08 01:46:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132234, 289002, 31443, '<td valign="top">Gísli! Congratulations! As I said before, simply beautiful!<br/>Stórkostlegt, til hamingju með bláa borðann!</td>', 'Gísli! Congratulations! As I said before, simply beautiful!Stórkostlegt, til hamingju með bláa borðann!', '2006-02-08 01:49:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132237, 288830, 41746, '<td valign="top">Stunning portrait. Well deserved. Til hamingju með gula borðann!</td>', 'Stunning portrait. Well deserved. Til hamingju með gula borðann!', '2006-02-08 01:50:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132241, 287519, 19831, '<td valign="top">This is a great choice for a subject I feel. I think the neutral tones could work well. Perhaps going for a different time of day, trying to get more of a raking light, could show off some texture. I agree about the focus, it does seem like it could be sharper. Depending on what editing software you have, maybe a little usm could help. There is good dof, blurring the background, but the main subject I think would be stronger if sharper. Also, in editing, some levels tweaking could strengthen the tonal range possibly. Centered compositions can work quite well with the right image, it isn''t bad here, but I''m thinking it might be a stronger presentation by not centering the subject in this case? <br/> <br/>Not totally terrible for a first entry :-), it could be a whole lot worse. You seem to have a good eye, you''ve isolated the subject well, and the shot seems to have purpose. It definitely doesn''t come across as just a ''snapshot''. I''m sure you''ll do well in the challenges, just keep shootin'' and have fun! <br/>:-)</td>', 'This is a great choice for a subject I feel. I think the neutral tones could work well. Perhaps going for a different time of day, trying to get more of a raking light, could show off some texture. I agree about the focus, it does seem like it could be sharper. Depending on what editing software you have, maybe a little usm could help. There is good dof, blurring the background, but the main subject I think would be stronger if sharper. Also, in editing, some levels tweaking could strengthen the tonal range possibly. Centered compositions can work quite well with the right image, it isn''t bad here, but I''m thinking it might be a stronger presentation by not centering the subject in this case?  Not totally terrible for a first entry :-), it could be a whole lot worse. You seem to have a good eye, you''ve isolated the subject well, and the shot seems to have purpose. It definitely doesn''t come across as just a ''snapshot''. I''m sure you''ll do well in the challenges, just keep shootin'' and have fun! :-)', '2006-02-08 01:51:43.000000', NULL, 0),
