(2132570, 289160, 18207, '<td valign="top">I''m surprised noone commented this one.<br/>Yes, there are two distracting elements: the bag(?) at the very top and the white line at the very bottom. Typing this post I became unsure of the distracting effect of the latter one, after all it''s in place. But on to the theme: even I -- being a European guy who are not used to watch baseball matches -- can identify one of the key postures of this sport. What''s even better, it is not the clishe posture. So I can say your choice is very good. The crop emphasizes it even more and the color tones give the feeling of baseball while keeping it real. Good work.<br/>PS. No, I''m not the one with the 10. :)</td>', 'I''m surprised noone commented this one.Yes, there are two distracting elements: the bag(?) at the very top and the white line at the very bottom. Typing this post I became unsure of the distracting effect of the latter one, after all it''s in place. But on to the theme: even I -- being a European guy who are not used to watch baseball matches -- can identify one of the key postures of this sport. What''s even better, it is not the clishe posture. So I can say your choice is very good. The crop emphasizes it even more and the color tones give the feeling of baseball while keeping it real. Good work.PS. No, I''m not the one with the 10. :)', '2006-02-08 04:19:38.000000', NULL, 0),
