(2132648, 281531, 37430, '<td valign="top"><i>Greetings from the Critique Club!</i> <br/> <br/><b>Aesthetic:</b>Ummm...I''m confused. I dont really know what I''m seeing here. I think this is night photo of the sky and drifting clouds have created the pattern. Somehow not very appealing. It took me few minutes to realize what I''m seeing and I''m sure many voters would have missed out on it in few seconds of glance during voting.<br/> <br/><b>Technical:</b> Silhoutte with dark background is not really my piece of cake. I know this might have been difficult shot, but is not a strong composition.<br/> <br/><b>Challenge:</b> Offcoure- Anything would fit into this them. So everything is good here :)<br/> <br/><b>Conclusion:</b> I feel the drifting clouds have created the pattern which is not very applealing. The photo really confuses (the single comments confirms that). I thought of stars to be dust on my screen and after wiping it off I thought it was some problem with camera. It took me long to realize it was stars. I feel the same photo, with some different angle to capture more of branches, taken during twilight or day time might have come out much better.<br/> <br/>I did the critique for your "blue" submission and I feel this one is not a full hearted effort ..or maybe its too confusing for the voters (incl me). You have really got some GREAT pictures in your profile and I dont this one fits amongst them.<br/> <br/>Wish you a great day!<br/><b><i>-Tej</i></b></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  Aesthetic:Ummm...I''m confused. I dont really know what I''m seeing here. I think this is night photo of the sky and drifting clouds have created the pattern. Somehow not very appealing. It took me few minutes to realize what I''m seeing and I''m sure many voters would have missed out on it in few seconds of glance during voting. Technical: Silhoutte with dark background is not really my piece of cake. I know this might have been difficult shot, but is not a strong composition. Challenge: Offcoure- Anything would fit into this them. So everything is good here :) Conclusion: I feel the drifting clouds have created the pattern which is not very applealing. The photo really confuses (the single comments confirms that). I thought of stars to be dust on my screen and after wiping it off I thought it was some problem with camera. It took me long to realize it was stars. I feel the same photo, with some different angle to capture more of branches, taken during twilight or day time might have come out much better. I did the critique for your "blue" submission and I feel this one is not a full hearted effort ..or maybe its too confusing for the voters (incl me). You have really got some GREAT pictures in your profile and I dont this one fits amongst them. Wish you a great day!-Tej', '2006-02-08 04:56:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132653, 288830, 36606, '<td valign="top">seriously good portrait. Love this style of portrait. I saw the resemblance to your photo too. Great work</td>', 'seriously good portrait. Love this style of portrait. I saw the resemblance to your photo too. Great work', '2006-02-08 04:57:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132658, 288830, 34956, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your yellow Egill. Frábær mynd.</td>', 'Congrats on your yellow Egill. Frábær mynd.', '2006-02-08 05:00:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2132660, 283763, 37430, '<td valign="top"><i>Greetings from the Critique Club!</i> <br/> <br/><b>Aesthetic:</b> You have got an eye for something as picturesque as this one but the image really lacks on many things.<br/> <br/><b>Technical:</b> The focus seems to be too soft. Also slower shutter speed would have helped capture more vivid colors.<br/> <br/><b>Challenge:</b> Anything would fit in "free study", so everything is good here :)<br/> <br/><b>Conclusion:</b> I feel this could have been great "posture" picture if the focus was sharp and colors were vivid. Somehow the photo seems to be right out of camera and had lots of potential for post-processing to make it really stand out. Try sharpening, contrast and some work with Hue/Saturation ...and you will really get a whole new picture from this one. I really feel tempted to try my hands on this one.<br/> <br/>I''m by no means expert in area of photography. My comments are purely based on my limited understanding of technology and art behind digital photography. Apart from doing detailed evaluation of your submission, my intent is to learn different styles  of photography by critically evaluating selective submissions. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via email or PM.<br/> <br/>Wish you a great day!<br/><b><i>-Tej</i></b></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  Aesthetic: You have got an eye for something as picturesque as this one but the image really lacks on many things. Technical: The focus seems to be too soft. Also slower shutter speed would have helped capture more vivid colors. Challenge: Anything would fit in "free study", so everything is good here :) Conclusion: I feel this could have been great "posture" picture if the focus was sharp and colors were vivid. Somehow the photo seems to be right out of camera and had lots of potential for post-processing to make it really stand out. Try sharpening, contrast and some work with Hue/Saturation ...and you will really get a whole new picture from this one. I really feel tempted to try my hands on this one. I''m by no means expert in area of photography. My comments are purely based on my limited understanding of technology and art behind digital photography. Apart from doing detailed evaluation of your submission, my intent is to learn different styles  of photography by critically evaluating selective submissions. If you''ve got any questions about this critique, please feel free to contact me via email or PM. Wish you a great day!-Tej', '2006-02-08 05:02:08.000000', NULL, 0),
